Shadow of Kingdoms is a free to play flash game that is a ripoff of another game.  It worked, looked ok, played ok, sounded ok, was understandable.   Another one of those build your Kingdom, then Attack and loot your neighboring players games.
Try it and delete it, it is terrible game.  I did NOT like it.   Play Imperia Online instead of this crap.
For more info;

Pros:
- build your own world(s), ship
- explore the infinite universe
- colonize
- large crafting content
Cons:
- repeatedly dive, dig, swim, walk a lot around/inside/at the bottom of not very diffent from each other plannets, gather fuel, find same kind of dungeons in every planet;
- sidequests are too casual;
- no npc's story depth (I find my crew shallow);
- keep fighting off eventual uninteligent metroidvania monsters;
- grind for gear, blueprints etc.;
- no character development;
- interact with alien communities, without getting too close to their essence and destiny.
Still, it's a +- 8.5/10 game in which more content is still being implemented.

- capital shoots silent arrows of mass destruction;
- ogres and angry trees use teleportation cheats and conquer my 200+ turns empire in 10 turns;
- advisor tells me how to end a turn after 20 turns;
- sent some units through a flashy portal, next turn all units got obliterated;
- priest hero one-shots enemy forts;
- rogue mass invasions.
100% Recommend!

